==Strategy==
This first stage is designed for you to learn about the boss in this Brutal Advent, Jumbo Jones, whom you can exploit for their drawn-out foreswing animation to stack huge amounts of damage in each of his respective stages. His knockback count is quite high relative to his HP, making it very easy to pull this off with adequately-leveled rushers.

His range gimmick makes it dangerous to use slow-moving attackers, as any unit caught in the second part of his Omni Strike will cause him to unleash a giant Wave Attack. Thankfully, this facilitates the use of short-ranged attackers like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to quickly rush down him and a majority of the boss wave threats. Bahamut will deal heavy damage to Jumbo Jones through his Explosion, enough to cripple both the Chibinel and Ragin' Gory that spawn alongside Jumbo Jones. Thankfully, Jumbo Jones' first hit deals just enough damage for Awakened Bahamut to survive with a sliver of HP left. He and other supplemental attackers like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]], [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]], and [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]], alongside several Research [[Cat Combo]]s, will prevent him from attacking ever again, though the use of the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] and [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] Battle Item is recommended in the event that he might.

The remaining supporting threats should pose no issue, and once Jumbo Jones is dead, the win is yours. If the initial chaining fails right before he dies, you can lure him to your base and chain him again with a combination of [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cats]], Bullet Train Cats, and/or Cafeteria Cats.

